# Sleep App — local environment template.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in your real keys.
# `.env.local` is gitignored; this template is checked in so a future
# clone of the repo knows what variables are expected.
#
# IMPORTANT: keys are loaded into the browser bundle via Vite. Anything
# prefixed with `VITE_` is exposed to client code. NEVER put a server-side
# secret in here -- if/when we add a backend, secrets go in the backend's
# environment, not Vite's. For v1 (single user, no backend) it's fine to
# bundle your personal keys into your local build, but do not deploy this
# build to friends without first reworking key handling (bring-your-own-key
# UI per brief section 8.3).

# Anthropic Claude API key. Used for sleep-story script generation.
# Paid tier (no quota worries during development).
VITE_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ElevenLabs API key. Used for v3 TTS narration.
# Free tier for now -- limited monthly characters; sufficient for testing
# Voice Design and a handful of stories per month.
VITE_ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# Long-form synthesis path for sleep stories. When `true` (default on
# Creator plan and up), scripts longer than ~4.5K chars go through the
# ElevenLabs Projects API which handles chunking server-side and returns
# a single audio file. When `false`, the app falls back to client-side
# chunked TTS + MP3 byte-concat. Stories at ~3K words are well past the
# 5K-char per-request limit of the standard TTS endpoint, so one of the
# two long-form paths is required for stories to render at all.
VITE_ELEVENLABS_USE_PROJECTS=true
